            <div xml:id="d390-a4">

                <pb facs="0743" n="681" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg681"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 to
                    inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from a report of Colonel Nuncio.</hi></head>
                <p>Inquiries have been made with regard to the damage done by Escobedo, Martinez,
                    and the American troops. A captain of military farmers accused Pepe Cárdenas to
                    the authorities <pb facs="0744" n="682" xml:id="pg682"/> of Eagle Pass as being
                    a revolutionary agent. An opportunity was never given to the accuser to present
                    his evidence, and the accused was acquitted, by what process no one knows.</p>
                <p>Cárdenas, Juan Reyes, and José Martinez organize and protect the revolutionists,
                    affording them shelter in their houses until they are ready to sally out on
                    their raids.</p>
            </div>
